["ERB Growth Model Development\nAnalyses and Results\nDamian Betebenner — Center for Assessment\n\nJanuary 9th, 2023","Data preparation\n• Current data being utilized for growth model proof of concept\n includes both CTP and Milestones:\n 2020 2021 2022\n Reading Comprehension CTP Fall 49,549 73,204 0\n\n Reading Comprehension CTP Spring 0 118,075 145,927\n\n Reading Comprehension MS Fall 11,380 17,902 0\n\n Reading Comprehension MS Winter 12,786 20,914 0\n\n Reading Comprehension MS Spring 0 6,523 12,371","Data preparation\n• LONG formatted data was produced as the first step in SGP\n analyses.\n• LEVEL was used as the indicator of GRADE\n• The R script utilized or data preparation is available here:","SGP Analyses\n• With data prepared, the next step is to run SGP analyses using\n this data.\n• Three sets of analyses were conducted based upon discussions of\n student test taking:\n • CTP to CTP: Fall to Fall and Spring to Spring\n • MS to MS: Fall to Winter, Fall to Spring, Winter to Spring\n • MS to CTP: Fall to Spring\n• Specifying these analyses is done through configurations available\n here.","SGP Analyses\n• As a first step we calculate SGPs for students based upon the\n configurations specified.\n• The SGP model utilized for ERB Reading Comprehension data takes\n account of:\n • The student’s prior score\n • The date in which the student took their test in the current window\n • The time span between when they took their current test and\n when they took their prior test\n• The R script utilized to run the SGP analyses is available here.","SGP Analyses\n• Analyses ran with no errors and SGPs were produced for all\n cohorts.\n• Once LEVEL was used instead of GRADE, everything lined up and\n worked\n• A selection of Goodness of fit results are presented on the\n following slides\n• Based upon cutscores provided by Adrienne, I updated the ERB\n meta-data in the SGP package. Those outscores and other meta-\n data can be found here.","SGP Results\n• Analyses ran with no errors and SGPs were produced for all\n cohorts.\n• Goodness of fit would benefit from larger sample sizes\n• Goodness of fit plots indicates some minor issues with ceilings\n on the exam (a few students repeatedly scoring perfectly on the\n exam).\n• Growth and achievement plots suggest an “unevenness” of the\n achievement level outscores","ERB: 2022 Reading (Spring) ERB: 2022 Reading (Spring)\n Norm & Criterion Referenced Growth & Achievement Norm & Criterion Referenced Growth & Achievement\n\n 1000 1000\n\n 90 90\n 950 950\n\n 900 900 75\n 75\n\n 850 850\n\n Percentile Growth Trajectory Percentile Growth Trajectory\n 800 800\n\n 750 750 50\n\n 700 50 700\n\n 650 99 650 99\n\nScale Score Scale Score\n 600 600\n\n 550 95 550 95\n\n 90 90 25\n 25\n 500 500\n 85 85\n\n 2022 Achievement Percentile 2022 Achievement Percentile\n 450 80 10 450 80 10\n 75 75\n 70 70\n 400 65 400 65\n 60 60\n 55 55\n 50 50\n 350 45 350 45\n 40 40\n 35 35\n 300 30 300 30\n 25 25\n 20 20\n 250 250\n 15 15\n\n 10 10\n 200 SGP trajectories\n SGP trajectories for\n for aa 1st\n 1st grade\n grade student\n student starting\n starting from\n from the\n the Level\n Level 1/Level\n 1/Level 22 cut.\n cut. 200 SGP trajectories\n SGP for aa 1st\n trajectories for 1st grade\n grade student\n student starting\n starting from\n from the\n the Level\n Level 2/Level\n 2/Level 33 cut.\n cut.\n 5 5\n\n Grade 1 Grade 2 Grade 3 Grade 4 Grade 5 Grade 6 Grade 7 Grade 8 Grade 9 Grade 10 Grade 1 Grade 2 Grade 3 Grade 4 Grade 5 Grade 6 Grade 7 Grade 8 Grade 9 Grade 10","Jonah Mitchell Sample School\n\nHow to interpret this student\ngrowth & achievement report Reading\n\n Scale Score\n Exceeds Expectations\n (Spring)\n Achievement\n\n Achievement Reading\n\n Levels (Spring)\n\n Scale Score\n Above Year's Growth\n\n Student Growth\n Growth\n Percentile Year's Growth Level Percentiles\n\n Meets Expectations\n\n Suggested Uses Below Year's Growth\n > Year's Growth 77th − 99th\n\n Review past growth to assess A